//! little-endian one byte per output element (`dequantize_row_iq3_s`,
//! `ggml-quants.c:2626-2641`, `(const uint8_t *)(iq3s_grid + idx)`). The
//! index is a 9-bit field -- the low 8 bits live in `qs`, the ninth in the
//! `qh` plane -- so this grid has twice the entries of `IQ3_XXS`'s own
